# request: "Data-flow diagram for the STRIDE review of checkout, with the trust
#  boundaries: DMZ, internal and data. The customer's browser sends
#  credentials to the login service and a card token to the checkout
#  service, both over HTTPS; they pass them on over mTLS to Auth and
#  Payments. Auth reads the password hash from the users DB; Payments sends
#  the token and amount to Stripe over HTTPS and writes the charge id to the
#  payments DB. The review is about the Payments process and the card token;
#  number the processes."
type: threat-model
reader: security reviewers in the STRIDE session
width: 800
direction: down
focus: internal.pay  # "the Payments process"
out: card entry in the browser (Stripe.js), sessions, logging, admin tools
nodes:
  browser: Customer browser
  dmz: DMZ
  dmz.login: 1. Login
  dmz.checkout: 2. Checkout
  internal: Internal
  internal.auth: 3. Auth
  internal.pay: 4. Payments
  data: Data
  data.users: Users DB {shape: cylinder}
  data.ledger: Payments DB {shape: cylinder}
  stripe: Stripe
edges:
  browser -> dmz.login: credentials\nHTTPS
  browser -> dmz.checkout: card token\nHTTPS
  dmz.login -> internal.auth: credentials\nmTLS
  dmz.checkout -> internal.pay: card token\nmTLS
  data.users -> internal.auth: password hash\nSQL
  internal.pay -> stripe: token,\namount\nHTTPS
  internal.pay -> data.ledger: charge id\nSQL
